# Help: Rust XArray implementation (rxarray)
#
# XARRAY_RUST builds rust/kernel/rxarray.rs, the Rust implementation of
# the XArray, into the kernel crate as kernel::rxarray. It is a
# reference implementation under evaluation next to the C XArray and
# does not yet cover every feature of the C one. The symbol is a bool,
# so there is nothing to load and no builtin/ counterpart.
#
# The symbol is not in mainline yet: it arrives with the Rust XArray
# series. On a tree without it the requested value is ignored, so the
# fragment is safe to carry.
#
# With test/kunit.config the kernel also carries the rust_rxarray KUnit
# suite, and with rust/rust-doctests.config the module's doctest.
# test/xarray-benchmark-rust.config inlines this symbol for the
# benchmark module that measures the implementation.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule: RUST and the
# RANDSTRUCT_NONE it requires (rust/rust.config sets the same pair).
# See: lib/Kconfig (XARRAY_RUST)
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/rust/
CONFIG_RANDSTRUCT_NONE=y
CONFIG_RUST=y
CONFIG_XARRAY_RUST=y
